Give the CPU nodes #cooling-cells, so the cpu-thermal cooling map can bind.

The other half of r193 makes the sensor read. This makes the reading do
something.

cpu-thermal declares a passive trip at 80C with a cooling map onto all four
CPUs:

	map0 {
		trip = <&target>;
		cooling-device = <&cpu0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
				 <&cpu1 ...>, <&cpu2 ...>, <&cpu3 ...>;
	};

but none of cpu@0..cpu@3 declares #cooling-cells, and
of_cpufreq_cooling_register() requires it: it looks the property up on the CPU's
device node and registers nothing at all when it is absent. So cpufreq-dt never
created a cooling device, the map had nothing to bind to, and
/sys/class/thermal contained zero cooling_deviceN entries - which is exactly
what was observed after r191 and written off as a side effect of the sensor
returning -ENODATA. It was not; it is independent, and it would have survived
the auxadc fix.

dtc had been saying so the whole time, on every build:

	Warning (cooling_device_property):
	/thermal-zones/cpu-thermal/cooling-maps/map0:
	Missing property '#cooling-cells' in node /cpus/cpu@0 or bad phandle
	(referred from cooling-device[0])

Without this the device still reads temperatures, and the 115C critical trip
still works - that one is handled by the thermal core directly rather than by a
cooling device, so there was always a backstop - but nothing throttles at the
80C passive trip, which is the entire point of a passive trip. Upstream
mt8173.dtsi carries #cooling-cells = <2> on its CPU nodes for this reason.

The GPU zone's maps reference &gpu, which already has #cooling-cells = <2> but
is status = "disabled", so those maps stay unbound. Separate question, left
alone here.

This goes in mt8163.dtsi rather than in the board dts because it describes the
SoC, not the board.

diff -urN '--exclude=.git' r193new/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163.dtsi r193cool/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163.dtsi
@@ -136,6 +136,7 @@
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_0>;
+			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 		};
 
 		cpu1: cpu@1 {
@@ -156,6 +157,7 @@
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_0>;
+			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 		};
 
 		cpu2: cpu@2 {
@@ -176,6 +178,7 @@
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_0>;
+			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 		};
 
 		cpu3: cpu@3 {
@@ -196,6 +199,7 @@
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_0>;
+			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 		};
 
 		cpu-map {
